Contract anchors required by Keel's vendor verifier:

- srt-launch-authority/v1
- LAUNCH_AUTHORITY_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS = 2_000
- EndpointLeaseRegistry.claimGeneration
- per-launch proxy authority requires a destination resolver
- state.draining = true
- launchLifecycleTail
- structurallyDeniesAllNetwork
- SRT_LAUNCH_AUTHORITY_CAPACITY
- stopLinuxBridgeProcess
- revoke(): Promise<void>
- release(): Promise<void>
- releaseLaunchFilesystemState
- filesystem mount state follows process settlement
- process exit retains mount sources while any sandbox count remains active
- failed wraps surrender only their invocation-owned mount paths
- generated nested-deny bind sources follow invocation ownership and settlement
- controller-owned reset replaces vendored process exit and signal hooks

This record is an inventory/contract patch because the Keel extension adds new files
and composes several earlier local patches. The exact reviewable diff is the Git commit
that adds this record; `VENDOR.md` documents rationale, security impact, compatibility,
evidence, and upstream status. `tools/vendor/verify-sandbox-runtime.mjs` pins SHA-256
postimages for every source and regression path listed above so later drift fails the
vendor gate until a new reviewed patch record updates those digests.
